The URL.revokeObjectURL(url) call happens immediately after the download is triggered with a.click(), which may cause the download to fail in some browsers if the browser hasn't started the download yet. Consider wrapping the revoke call in a setTimeout with a small delay (e.g., 100ms) to ensure the browser has time to begin the download before the URL is revoked. This is a common best practice for programmatic downloads to avoid race conditions.
```suggestion
      setTimeout(() => {
        URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
      }, 100);
```

